0..65 Comment "// A bound over a recursion that may not end holds at each clock."
66..68 Comment "//"
69..143 Comment "// A run under `Partial` that does not end has no count. So a bound over a"
144..218 Comment "// partial program holds at each clock: the unfolding that stops after `n`"
219..294 Comment "// passes. That unfolding recurses on its clock, and conversion decides its"
295..372 Comment "// count. A run that ends after `k` passes is its unfolding at every clock of"
373..430 Comment "// `k` or more. So the bounds at each clock cover it too."
431..433 Comment "//"
434..509 Comment "// Conversion never unfolds a partial fixpoint, so a partial run\'s count is"
510..562 Comment "// never a path endpoint. The run itself reports it."
563..565 Comment "//"
566..644 Comment "// - see: `../../../library/std/src/cost.gandr` — `Cost.Eff`, `Counting` and"
645..675 Comment "//   the reading at each clock"
676..749 Comment "// - see: `../../ledger/features/cost-effect.gandr` — a closed bound by"
750..765 Comment "//   conversion"
766..841 Comment "// - see: `../../sketch/cost/partial.gandr` — a potential under `Partial`"
